      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think i may have found a potential solution.\n\nChanging updateValueInDom:\n\n```\n  private async updateValueInDom() {\n    const editableDivElement \u003d\n      this.editableDivElement ?? (await this.editableDiv);\n    if (editableDivElement) {\n      if (this.contentEditableAttributeValue \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027true\u0027 || this.contentEditableAttributeValue \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027\u0027) {\n        const lines \u003d (this.value ?? \u0027\u0027).split(\u0027\\n\u0027);\n        editableDivElement.innerHTML \u003d lines\n          .map(line \u003d\u003e line ? `\u003cdiv\u003e${htmlEscape(line)}\u003c/div\u003e` : \u0027\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u0027)\n          .join(\u0027\u0027);\n      } else {\n        editableDivElement.innerText \u003d this.value || \u0027\u0027;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  \n  private get contentEditableAttributeValue() {\n    if (this.disabled) {\n      return \u0027false\u0027;\n    }\n\n    if (this.isPlaintextOnlySupported) {\n      if (/firefox/i.test(navigator.userAgent)) {\n        return \u0027\u0027;\n      }\n      return \u0027plaintext-only\u0027 as unknown as \u0027true\u0027;\n    }\n\n    return \u0027true\u0027;\n  }\n```\n\nI dunno if this is acceptable cc @brohlfs@google.com? It works for me in firefox and it escapes the html.",
